WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.200
Earth's Mightiest Parodies might be making an&nbsp;
appearance in the new season of "The Boys."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.640
Will Hughie get some Payback?&nbsp;
Will Homelander be creepy?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:11.680
And is Tek Knight going to explode&nbsp;
onto the scene this season?

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:16.560
One of the most exciting additions to&nbsp;
"The Boys" Season 3 is Soldier Boy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:21.520
played by "Supernatural" star Jensen Ackles.&nbsp;
But as tends to be the case with new Supes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:25.360
on "The Boys," there's likely more to&nbsp;
this character than first meets the eye.

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:29.760
As one can guess from his uniform and name,&nbsp;
Soldier Boy is effectively a stand-in for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:35.120
Captain America in this universe. His personal&nbsp;
history even dates him back to World War II,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:40.320
much like Cap from the world of Marvel. But the&nbsp;
allusions seemingly go much deeper than that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:44.480
At one point in the trailer, we see a&nbsp;
person sitting in front of papers on a wall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:49.200
one of which is a newspaper with a headline&nbsp;
that refers to "Our Fallen Soldier Boy."

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:54.640
In the comics, the public is misled about Soldier&nbsp;
Boy's origins. The original who fought in WWII&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:59.360
actually died in the line of duty, while the&nbsp;
modern day incarnation is simply a replacement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:04.320
masquerading as the original. Of course, the&nbsp;
show's zagged comic fans in the past. Could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:08.960
this version actually be the original? Or perhaps&nbsp;
it's already known in the world of Amazon's "The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:14.160
Boys" that Soldier Boy is a legacy title. It could&nbsp;
make for a particularly timely development seeing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:18.960
how the mantle of Captain America has recently&nbsp;
switched bearers in the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:25.280
Jensen Ackles' Soldier Boy isn't the only new&nbsp;
Supe coming to "The Boys" Season 3, as the trailer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:30.480
gives fans a look at "The Walking Dead" alum&nbsp;
Laurie Holden as the Crimson Countess, a parody&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:34.960
of Marvel's Scarlet Witch. In the trailer,&nbsp;
we see this new hero throwing a red energy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:40.320
blast at someone dressed as Homelander, which&nbsp;
makes them explode into a million gory pieces.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:45.280
In the comics, Crimson Countess is a member of&nbsp;
Payback, the second most popular team in "The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:50.000
Boys" universe after the Seven. If the Seven&nbsp;
are clear stand-ins for the Justice League,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:54.240
Payback is basically the Avengers. It's&nbsp;
worth noting that Stormfront is also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:59.360
on Payback in the source material, and Aya&nbsp;
Cash played the fascist villain in Season 2.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:03.360
So, it's possible we could see a whole&nbsp;
team of Avenger parodies in season 3.

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:08.240
After watching "The Boys" Season 3&nbsp;
trailer, it's clear that the show is not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:12.880
shying away from parodying major real-life&nbsp;
political moments in its upcoming season.

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:17.920
Firstly, we see A-Train show up at a protest&nbsp;
seemingly to help keep the peace ... only to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:22.160
pull out and promote a soda called Turbo&nbsp;
Rush. For those familiar with a certain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:27.760
viral moment starring Kendall Jenner and a&nbsp;
Pepsi can, the image looks familiar. In 2017,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:32.000
Jenner starred in an ad for Pepsi, in which&nbsp;
she hands a can of the soft drink to a police&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:36.400
officer staring down a group of protestors,&nbsp;
which elicits applause from the crowd.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:40.400
The ad was soon pulled for seeming to&nbsp;
trivialize the Black Lives Matter movement,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:43.760
as reported by the New York&nbsp;
Times. As "The Boys" points out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:47.360
some public figures — or large soda&nbsp;
companies — will bank on any kind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:52.240
of well-known movement to advertise their&nbsp;
products – whether it's appropriate or not.

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:56.480
Secondly, in one short clip, we see a&nbsp;
crowd of Homelander fans holding signs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.480 --> 00:03:00.800
in support of the leader of the Seven. One of&nbsp;
the members of the crowd is wearing a headdress&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:07.040
with horns — just like Jacob Chansley, aka the&nbsp;
QAnon Shaman of the January 6 Capitol Riots.

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:12.160
Right at 27 seconds into this latest&nbsp;
trailer for "The Boys" Season 3,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:16.280
amidst a number of newspaper clippings&nbsp;
about various superhero activities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:20.480
is a headline that reads: "Woman&nbsp;
Paralyzed in Tek Knight Hostage Rescue."

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:24.400
Viewers with knowledge of "The Boys" comic&nbsp;
series should remember Tek Knight as a sort&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:29.360
of exaggerated mashup of Batman and Iron&nbsp;
Man. Just like the two heroes that serve as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:33.200
the basis for his character, Tek&nbsp;
Knight has no superpowers of his own,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:37.440
which also sets him apart from most of&nbsp;
the Supes in the universe of "The Boys."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:41.840
Instead, he relies on a mechanical&nbsp;
suit to accomplish super-heroic feats.

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:45.680
This isn't the first time "The Boys" has&nbsp;
teased the introduction of Tek Knight.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:48.320
Previously, perhaps alluding to the same incident,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:52.160
a woman at a support group revealed&nbsp;
that Tek Knight damaged her spine.

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:55.760
"I know it's wrong to be angry.&nbsp;
After all, Tek Knight saved me.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:01.840
I just wish he'd been a little&nbsp;
more gentle with my spine."

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:06.640
Despite the hints, Tek Knight has yet to appear&nbsp;
in the live-action adaptation of "The Boys." Could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:12.000
his appearance finally come in Season 3? A bigger&nbsp;
question for those who've read the comics may be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:16.320
whether the Tek Knight of the show has the same&nbsp;
"issues" that his comics counterpart suffers from.

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:21.840
It seems that the 3rd season of "The Boys" will be&nbsp;
venturing further into the pages of the comic book&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:26.320
the show is based on. Besides the appearance&nbsp;
of Soldier Boy and mentions of Tek Knight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:31.200
a significant takeaway from this preview may be&nbsp;
that Butcher and his team are finally going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:35.840
get powered up. If that's the case, it will&nbsp;
no doubt change the playing field forever.

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:39.360
Among the blink or you'll miss them moments,&nbsp;
there is some evidence that our favorite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:44.800
gang of Supe-killers may be taking their own&nbsp;
version of the Supe-creating serum Compound V.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:49.440
Besides showing Butcher testing out heat vision&nbsp;
that could match even a staredown with Homelander,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:52.880
we also see him throwing up all&nbsp;
over Hughie, whose track record&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:57.680
of being covered in some form of unspeakable&nbsp;
fluid looks to be untarnished this season.

00:04:57.680 --> 00:05:00.880
Interestingly, the teaser also&nbsp;
shows The Boys' newest recruit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:04.880
enduring his arm being brutally&nbsp;
snapped and Butcher not batting an eye.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:09.200
Could the reaction be down to the fact&nbsp;
that Hughie also takes some V? Perhaps,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:14.080
or maybe he's just getting some very unfortunate&nbsp;
preparation done for an undercover assignment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:19.680
Either way, looks like Hughie's in for some&nbsp;
pain when the new season drops on June 3, 2022.

